<task id="111" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>ISS-021 (#1000) — the org-baseline read is an unbounded N+1 on the authorization hot path</title>
    <phase>Register-driven (queued 2026-09-18 by owner directive)</phase>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Evaluator hot path (.cs); tags bff-api/auth; modifies tests.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>A bounded performance change with an existing precedent to copy (the membership walk's `Capped` surfacing) and a named escalation for the one design choice. Unchanged from the stub: premise verification did not widen the blast radius — it narrowed it, by showing the guard tests do not pin this path.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>medium</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/** is parallel-unsafe in this project; this also edits the shared `ISubjectStandingGrantReader` seam.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>043</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3–4 hours</estimated-effort>
    <origin>Register ISS-021 / GitHub #1000. Filed by task 043 Step 9.5 code-review finding M-3. Queued by the owner's 2026-09-18 directive. Authored 2026-09-19 with premises re-verified against HEAD — one register claim was FALSE, see `&lt;notes&gt;`.</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>`AccessibleRecordSetService.ComposeForContactAsync` (`:1114`) awaits one `ISubjectStandingGrantReader.ReadForOrganizationAsync` per distinct active organization, SERIALLY — `foreach` at `:1200`, `await` at `:1215-1216` — and each call is a single-row Dataverse retrieve (`SubjectStandingGrantReader.cs:164-166`). The org id list comes from `QueryActiveOrgIdsAsync`, which applies no `$top` (`ExternalParticipationService.cs:1092-1094`), so N is unbounded by construction. `IsRecordAccessibleAsync` (`:758`) and `IsOperationPermittedAsync` (`:794`) each call `ComposeAsync`, and `ComposeAsync` (`:728-745`) is a bare switch with no cache — so the cost is paid again on every authorization decision.

🔴 **Correct the register's cost claim before you scope the work.** ISS-021 says "zero organisations hold a standing grant, so N is currently 0 and the loop never executes." **The loop DOES execute.** It iterates the contact's ACTIVE ORG MEMBERSHIPS (`:1200`), and the `Rights == None` skip happens AFTER the read (`:1218-1221`). Standing grants decide only whether a membership WALK follows — never whether the READ happens. So the round trips are paid per active org membership even when no organization holds a standing grant, which is the current state. Re-measure N yourself; do not inherit either number.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer, C#/.NET, the external access evaluator.</role>
  <goal>The org-baseline read is bounded and does not scale with the number of organizations on the authorization hot path — either one batched query for N organization ids, or an explicit bound whose truncation is VISIBLE per NFR-03 rather than silent.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>The org-expansion term is task 043's (design §4.5 term 4 / FR-24 + FR-25). The read it loops over is task 042's level-bearing seam. The N+1 is structural, not a bug in either: `ReadForOrganizationAsync` is per-subject BY CONSTRUCTION (one `IGenericEntityService.RetrieveAsync` per call, `IGenericEntityService.cs:12`), so bounding it means either a new batched read or an explicit cap.

Batching IS feasible on the existing client — `IGenericEntityService.RetrieveMultipleAsync(QueryExpression, ct)` at `IGenericEntityService.cs:70` supports one query over N ids (`ConditionOperator.In`). No new client, package or interface-family is needed; at most one method on the existing reader.

The `Capped` precedent to copy, rather than inventing a second shape: `AccessibleRecordSet.Capped` (`:138`) plus `CapCeiling` (`:141-142`) so a caller renders the NFR-03 message without hard-coding the number, `MembershipPageWalk` (`:811`), and the walk's own cap sites (`:904-956`). Spec NFR-03 is at `spec.md:132`.

⚠️ Verified NOT a constraint: `tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/ExternalAccessQueryIntegrityGuardTests.cs` does not reference `ReadForOrganizationAsync` or the standing-grant reader at all, so this change does not have to satisfy that guard. Do not assume it does.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/AccessibleRecordSetService.cs (the org loop, :1197-1249)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/SubjectStandingGrantReader.cs (only if the chosen shape is a batched read — the interface is at :79-104)</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/AccessibleRecordSetServiceTests.cs (the org-expansion region, :1386-1496)</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/SubjectStandingGrantReaderTests.cs (only if the reader gains a method)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/AccessibleRecordSetService.cs:780-960 (WalkMembershipPagesAsync — the existing bound-and-surface-Capped implementation to copy)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="NFR-03">Scope: truncation. A truncated read must be visibly truncated, never silently. Reuse the existing `Capped` + `CapCeiling` surfacing rather than inventing a second shape.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Scope: fail direction. Fail closed. A batched read that partially fails must not resolve to "fewer organizations confer" — that is a silent under-grant on the additive term, and the existing per-org behaviour already fails closed to `Rights == None` per organization (`:1218-1221`). Preserve that: one unreadable organization must not decide the others.</constraint>
    <constraint source="register ISS-021 (CORRECTED)">Scope: the cost claim. Do NOT repeat "N is currently 0". N is the count of ACTIVE ORG MEMBERSHIPS, not of standing-grant holders, and the read is unconditional per membership. Re-measure and record what you measured.</constraint>
    <constraint source="task 042">Scope: the seam's contract. `ReadForOrganizationAsync`'s fail-closed contract and its `isFlsSecured: false` asymmetry versus the contact read (`SubjectStandingGrantReader.cs:148-152`) are deliberate and live-verified. A batched read must keep the same fail-closed value per subject and must not silently adopt the contact path's FLS log wording.</constraint>
    <constraint source="task 043">Scope: the single-snapshot invariant. The ONE junction read shared by the additive term and the deny-veto subject (`:1134-1137`) must stay one read. Do not add a second org query while removing the N+1 — that trades a bounded cost for the two-snapshot hazard 043 deliberately removed.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11">Scope: new surface. Prefer extending the existing reader over a new service or interface family. If the chosen shape adds a method, it replaces the loop — the per-org method must not survive as a second way to do the same thing unless a caller still needs it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: this task's PR. Placement Justification; publish size versus a FRESH master worktree (hazards 3 + 4 — short paths, equal file counts on both sides); no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="review-2026-08-24">Scope: verification. Pair positives with negatives; perturbation is mandatory.</constraint>
  </constraints>

