  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The measured N is recorded in the notes, with its definition stated (active org memberships, not standing-grant holders) and whether it came from live Dataverse or from the 2026-08-26 prior.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A contact with N greater than 1 active org memberships resolves the org baseline without one Dataverse round trip per organization — or, if the bound shape was chosen, with the ceiling applied and `Capped` true.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The composed rights are UNCHANGED by this task for every existing org-expansion case: per-organization baseline levels, the at-most-three walks bucketed by distinct baseline, and Secure suppression of the derived term.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative case preserved: a contact belonging to NO organization performs no org-baseline read at all and sets `Sources.OrgExpansionMembership` false (the meaning of the current `Times.Never` assertion at `AccessibleRecordSetServiceTests.cs:1493-1495`).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Fail-closed, per subject: an organization whose row is missing, whose flag is unreadable, or whose baseline is unset contributes NOTHING, and does not prevent the other organizations in the same read from contributing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Fail-closed, whole read: a transport-level failure of the batched read contributes nothing and never resolves to "fewer organizations confer" reported as success.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Authorization outcome unchanged at the two entry points: `IsRecordAccessibleAsync` and `IsOperationPermittedAsync` return the same answers as before for an org-derived record, including the `requiredRights == None` caller-bug denial (`AccessibleRecordSetService.cs:784-792`).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">If the bound shape was chosen: truncation is visible — `Capped` is true and `CapCeiling` carries the ceiling, per NFR-03, and a test asserts the flag rather than only the id count.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">If a batched method was added: the per-organization loop is gone from the evaluator, and no second code path reads the org baseline one id at a time unless a caller still requires it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Perturbation: reverting to the per-organization loop (or removing the bound) fails at least one test; and making the batched read fail closed to "all organizations confer" instead of "none" fails at least one test.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build green; full suite green; ArchTests green; publish size reported against a fresh master worktree and ≤60 MB.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Authored 2026-09-19. Premises re-verified against HEAD; one register claim is FALSE and is corrected in `&lt;prompt&gt;` + the constraints.

**VERIFIED TRUE** — serial per-org await (`AccessibleRecordSetService.cs:1200` foreach, `:1215-1216` await); each call is one single-row retrieve (`SubjectStandingGrantReader.cs:164-166` via `IGenericEntityService.cs:12`); no `$top` on the org id query (`ExternalParticipationService.cs:1092-1094`); no composition-level cache (`ComposeAsync` `:728-745` is a bare switch; `IsRecordAccessibleAsync` `:758` and `IsOperationPermittedAsync` `:794` each call it per check); the `Capped` precedent exists (`:138`, `:141-142`, `:811`, `:904-956`).

**VERIFIED FALSE — the register's urgency rationale.** `defer-issues.md:695-696`: *"zero organisations hold a standing grant, so N is currently 0 and the loop never executes."* The loop iterates active ORG MEMBERSHIPS (`:1200`) and the `Rights == None` skip is AFTER the read (`:1218-1221`), so the reads are paid per membership regardless of standing grants. Live evidence contradicts N=0 outright: `notes/task-020-org-grant-spe-cleanup.md` §1 (live Dataverse 2026-08-26) records *"2 active membership rows across 2 organizations; active org grants exist for `Morrison Foerster LLP`, which has an active member."* Two Ns were conflated: reads scale with memberships, WALKS scale with standing-grant holders. The task stays low priority — the wasted reads are small and return nothing — but "the cost is unpaid" is not true, and the remediation plan's "safe alone because N is 0" rests on the same conflation.

Sequencing: 111 touches the ORG-ID CONSUMER, and the direct call is `ReadActiveOrgMembershipsAsync` (`:1137`, body `:486-516`) which delegates to `QueryActiveOrgIdsAsync` (`:500`). Tasks 109/110 rewrite that query to return an outcome plus two named sets. If 109/110 land first, rebase onto their shape and read the org ids from it. This task must NOT change the junction query itself.

Related: tasks 042 (the seam), 043 (the term + the single-snapshot invariant), 105 (collection-read rewrite — check for overlap before starting), 109/110 (the same org-id read).</notes>

